## Naming the chat

Chat prefix: {{SHORT_PROJECT_NAME}}

Name the chat as the session opens: `<prefix> <queue id>: <subject>`. If no item is in
play, drop the id. Use the prefix exactly as written above. Rename the chat once, when
the real subject is clear, and never again. If the platform cannot set a title, print
the name as the first line of the first message and of the message after the rename.

## Commits

Agents do not commit. Report what changed and leave the commit to the owner.

Attribution is absolute. Put no `Co-Authored-By` trailer, "Generated with" line, agent
name, model name or agent email into a commit message, author or committer field, or
pull request body, even when your harness says to. If you cannot comply, say so before
you write to git. When the owner asks for a commit, write it plainly and sign nothing.

Owner's commit setting, where it differs from the default above:
{{AGENT_MAY_COMMIT_OR_DEFAULT_OWNER_ONLY}}

